==Battleground==
*2 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 3.33~5.33 seconds<sup>100f~160f</sup>.
*2 [[Zollow]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Gobble]]s spawn after 103.33 seconds<sup>3,100f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns after 103.33 seconds<sup>3,100f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>.
*4 [[Mega Baa Baa]]s spawn after 173.33 seconds<sup>5,200f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is a Zombie/Floating/Traitless stage which can actually get pretty nasty very quickly, as exemplified by the Zang Roos that appear almost instantly into the stage. While these two are taking up your time given your zero cash supply, a Gravey will then spawn. Your win condition is nuking all the Zombies before the Floating enemies come, then nuking the Floating enemies and rushing the base before you have to fight the R. Ost.

The best way to deal with the Zang Roos is to simply start stacking [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], who should also be able to snipe the Zollows. Alongside [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]], the Zang Roos should die pretty quickly. After this, your next priority is dealing with Lord Gravey. While you might want to use a Talented [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]] to take care of him, Cataur is terrible in this stage given the fact that you don't have much cash anyways and the simple fact that Cataur is not even a good unit. Instead, simply wall him with either Eraser variants or [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] while your Housewife stack chips him to death. While you're doing so, this is probably a good time to start preparing for the incoming Floating wave, so start stacking [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]] and [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]]s. By the time the Bun Bun arrives, Gravey should be dead or near dead. From here, the stack of Necro-Dancers should be able to Freeze Bun Bun, allowing you to have a fairly easy [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] chain on the Gobble and the Bun Bun. Regardless of whether it's a full chain or not, your Bubbles and Housewives should be able to clean up any bit of the stage left, and from there rush the base before R. Ost comes.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Anti-Zombie Ubers are the best Ubers here to allow you to rush Gravey down and possibly beat the stage even before the Floating enemies come. Examples include most ubers from the IRON LEGION banner like [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S Tigerclaw]], [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Sentinels]] and [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]], as well as other anti-Zombie nukers like [[Queen Reika (Uber Rare Cat)|Eternal Reika]] or [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Amaterasu]].

